THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
================================================================================

This is the bootstrap summary of third-party and derived-source obligations for
the Swift port of Open Grok. It retains the derived-source provenance (source
revisions, copyrights, upstream URLs, and versions) captured from the
read-only Rust reference at /tmp/open-grok-reference so that the obligations
are self-contained at the repository root before any owning target lands.

The complete, machine-generated transitive license inventory (matching
Package.resolved, vendored code, and assets) is produced and audited by the
W11-S5 release-validation slice and embedded in release artifacts and the
in-product notices view. The Swift package currently declares no external
dependencies; transitive-package obligations accrue as later waves pin and
audit non-Foundation dependencies (SQLite C API, JavaScript engine, syntax
grammars, compression/crypto as needed), each wrapped in an OpenGrok target
with its license/source revision recorded here and in the per-target NOTICE
files as those targets are integrated.

